  "query_preview": "..\nWeak trade wind showers are making their way over the Marianas this\nafternoon. Moisture is expected to stay high enough for this pattern\nto continue for much of the week. Winds should be light enough for \nisland effect showers to develop over the west side of Guam from Apra\nHarbor south to Malesso, so scattered showers are in the forecast \nfor that area. Scattered showers are expected for all the Marianas by\nWednesday due to further weakening of the winds and potentially \nincreased moisture from a trade wind trough moving through. Island\neffect showers may continue through the end of the week if moisture \nis sufficient enough.",
